---
title: Classic Pita
source: https://www.bengingi.com/recipe/classic-pita/
tags:
    - bread
servings: 8
---

In a bowl mix {water `lukewarm`: 300lt } and {dry yeast: 10gr}. Add {sugar: 25gr} and mix well.

Add the {flour `0`: 500gr} and mix all the ingredients until there is almost no flour
remaining in the bowl. Add {salt: 10gr}. Move the dough out of the bowl and knead it on a work surface.

Knead dough manually for about 7 to 10 minutes until smooth and sexy ;)
If the dough is dry, feel free to wet your hands and the flour will absorb easily.

Round and place the dough in a bowl and cover with a towel. Let the dough rest until
nearly double the volume.

Divide into 100-120 gr pieces. Round each piece into a perfect tight ball and let sit for 10 min,
covered with a towel.

With a rolling pin open the Pitas to 0.5 cm thick. Place the Pitas to proof on a towel for 20 min.

Heat a large strong pan over medium heat for 3-5 min. Lower the heat to low-medium and bake the pita
on the side that touched the towel before.

After 10 sec turn to the other side. Another 10 sec and turn back.
And this is how you play with the Pita until you get a stunning pocket.

Move the pita to a basket/bowl covered with a towel that will avoid the Pita from drying.

